            <ArticleTitle>[Otolaryngologic symptoms from tumors of the posterior cranial fossa].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>158-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of the paper was the estimation of the otolaryngological signs in the patients with the tumor of posterior cranial cavity. Each one was underwent the otoneurological diagnosis inclusive of electronystagmography. The most frequent symptoms we noticed were headache, vertigo together with cerebellar signs and disorder of the VII, VIII and IX-th cranial nerves, The ENG seemed to be a useful method in a localizing process of intracranial damages.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
